{"id":"stmt:sato2009@pdftotext-pieces/l0003-05","source":"source:sato2009","asset":"asset:sato2009@pdftotext-pieces","locator":{"leaf":3,"printed":null,"section":null,"example":null},"anchor":{"exact":"ciki は益岡の「個別的事態」の仮定を表すが、その際、文末のムードに制約があ\nり、原則として疑問、命令のムードが現れる。","match":1,"method":"exact","leaf":3},"statement":{"en":"The conjunction ciki expresses a hypothesis of an individual event, and is subject to a mood constraint such that the main clause in principle takes an interrogative or imperative mood.","ja":"ciki は個別的事態の仮定を表すが、文末のムードに制約があり、原則として疑問または命令のムードが現れる。"},"type":"distribution","stance":"asserts","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/chitose"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"hedge":null,"reported":null,"forms":["ciki"],"topics":["topic:complex/conditional-temporal-concessive-clauses","topic:complex/conditional-temporal-concessive-clauses--ciki"],"extracted_by":"act:extract/sato2009/2026-09-10T14-36-38-832Z","verification":{"anchor":"pass","image":"not-applicable","entailment":{"verdict":"yes","quote":"ciki は益岡の「個別的事態」の仮定を表すが、その際、文末のムードに制約があり、原則として疑問、命令のムードが現れる。","note":null,"model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","prompt_version":"verify-v1.0","date":"2026-09-10"},"human":null},"status":"checked","routing":{"section":"topic:complex/conditional-temporal-concessive-clauses--ciki","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","prompt_version":"route-v1.0","date":"2026-09-10"}}
{"id":"stmt:sato2009@pdftotext-pieces/l0003-06","source":"source:sato2009","asset":"asset:sato2009@pdftotext-pieces","locator":{"leaf":3,"printed":null,"section":null,"example":null},"anchor":{"exact":"kor は益岡の「一般的な因果関係」を表すのに用いられる","match":1,"method":"exact","leaf":3},"statement":{"en":"The conjunction kor is used to express general causal relationships.","ja":"kor は一般的な因果関係を表すのに用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","stance":"asserts","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/chitose"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"hedge":null,"reported":null,"forms":["kor"],"topics":["topic:complex/conditional-temporal-concessive-clauses","topic:complex/conditional-temporal-concessive-clauses--kor-conditional"],"extracted_by":"act:extract/sato2009/2026-09-10T14-36-38-832Z","verification":{"anchor":"pass","image":"not-applicable","entailment":{"verdict":"yes","quote":"kor は益岡の「一般的な因果関係」を表すのに用いられる","note":null,"model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","prompt_version":"verify-v1.0","date":"2026-09-10"},"human":null},"status":"checked","routing":{"section":"topic:complex/conditional-temporal-concessive-clauses--kor-conditional","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","prompt_version":"route-v1.0","date":"2026-09-10"}}
{"id":"stmt:sato2009@pdftotext-pieces/l0003-07","source":"source:sato2009","asset":"asset:sato2009@pdftotext-pieces","locator":{"leaf":3,"printed":null,"section":null,"example":null},"anchor":{"exact":"kor は益岡の「個別的事態」の仮定を表すのにも用いられる。ただし、文末にはムード\nの制約があり、疑問詞疑問文で用いられるのが通例である","match":1,"method":"exact","leaf":3},"statement":{"en":"The conjunction kor is also used to express hypotheses of individual events, but with a constraint on the clause-final mood, usually appearing in wh-interrogative sentences.","ja":"kor は個別的事態の仮定を表すのにも用いられるが、文末にはムードの制約があり、疑問詞疑問文で用いられるのが通例である。"},"type":"distribution","stance":"asserts","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/chitose"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"hedge":null,"reported":null,"forms":["kor"],"topics":["topic:complex/conditional-temporal-concessive-clauses","topic:complex/conditional-temporal-concessive-clauses--kor-conditional"],"extracted_by":"act:extract/sato2009/2026-09-10T14-36-38-832Z","verification":{"anchor":"pass","image":"not-applicable","entailment":{"verdict":"yes","quote":"kor は益岡の「個別的事態」の仮定を表すのにも用いられる。ただし、文末にはムードの制約があり、疑問詞疑問文で用いられるのが通例である。","note":null,"model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","prompt_version":"verify-v1.0","date":"2026-09-10"},"human":null},"status":"checked","routing":{"section":"topic:complex/conditional-temporal-concessive-clauses--kor-conditional","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","prompt_version":"route-v1.0","date":"2026-09-10"}}
{"id":"stmt:sato2009@pdftotext-pieces/l0003-08","source":"source:sato2009","asset":"asset:sato2009@pdftotext-pieces","locator":{"leaf":3,"printed":null,"section":null,"example":null},"anchor":{"exact":"yak は後に pirka「良い」、wen「悪い」を取って","match":1,"method":"exact","leaf":3},"statement":{"en":"The conjunction yak is frequently used with pirka 'good' or wen 'bad' following it, forming idiomatic expressions meaning 'one should do' or 'one must not do'.","ja":"yak は後に pirka「良い」、wen「悪い」を取って、「すれば良い」、「してはいけない」のような慣用句的表現をなして用いられることが多い。"},"type":"form-function","stance":"asserts","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/chitose"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"hedge":null,"reported":null,"forms":["yak","pirka","wen"],"topics":["topic:complex/conditional-temporal-concessive-clauses","topic:complex/conditional-temporal-concessive-clauses--yak-yakne"],"extracted_by":"act:extract/sato2009/2026-09-10T14-36-38-832Z","verification":{"anchor":"pass","image":"not-applicable","entailment":{"verdict":"yes","quote":"yak は後に pirka「良い」、wen「悪い」を取って、「すれば良い」、「してはいけない」のような慣用句的表現をなして用いられることが多い。","note":null,"model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","prompt_version":"verify-v1.0","date":"2026-09-10"},"human":null},"status":"checked","routing":{"section":"topic:complex/conditional-temporal-concessive-clauses--yak-yakne","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","prompt_version":"route-v1.0","date":"2026-09-10"}}
{"id":"stmt:sato2009@pdftotext-pieces/l0003-09","source":"source:sato2009","asset":"asset:sato2009@pdftotext-pieces","locator":{"leaf":3,"printed":null,"section":null,"example":null},"anchor":{"exact":"聞き手に対する働きかけの意味を含んでいるのが\n通例なので、これも一種の文末のムードに関する制約と言えるであろう。","match":1,"method":"exact","leaf":3},"statement":{"en":"Clauses marked with yak are typically subject to a mood-like constraint in that they usually convey an appeal or directive toward the addressee.","ja":"yak は聞き手に対する働きかけの意味を含んでいるのが通例であり、これも一種の文末のムードに関する制約と言える。"},"type":"distribution","stance":"asserts","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/chitose"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"hedge":null,"reported":null,"forms":["yak"],"topics":["topic:complex/conditional-temporal-concessive-clauses","topic:complex/conditional-temporal-concessive-clauses--yak-yakne"],"extracted_by":"act:extract/sato2009/2026-09-10T14-36-38-832Z","verification":{"anchor":"pass","image":"not-applicable","entailment":{"verdict":"yes","quote":"聞き手に対する働きかけの意味を含んでいるのが通例なので、これも一種の文末のムードに関する制約と言えるであろう。","note":null,"model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","prompt_version":"verify-v1.0","date":"2026-09-10"},"human":null},"status":"checked","routing":{"section":"topic:complex/conditional-temporal-concessive-clauses--yak-yakne","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","prompt_version":"route-v1.0","date":"2026-09-10"}}
